# Where proofs are checked, the row of a copy that was found under a key is held in the turn against the operation that finds an own value of a plain object under a TEXT (holdRowRememberedAgainstReadInTurn()).
# An ELEMENT remembered of a list under a counter lies under the same kind of note. Held against that operation it reads "absent": this right program stopped under testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime and --aot-harden=proof-checks
# The check is built for the row of the copy alone; every other remembered answer is walked a second time, as before.
